{"id":31903,"path":"/grammar-points/shorts/if-vs-whether-grammar-shorts/","parentId":30685,"order":925,"section":"grammar-points","level":null,"depth":3,"title":"If vs Whether – Grammar Shorts","seo":{"title":"If vs Whether – Grammar Shorts - Test-English","description":"Learn the difference between 'if' and 'whether' with our grammar lesson that includes a clear explanation, a grammar chart and an exercise!","image":"/media/uploads/If-vs-Whether-Grammar-shorts.webp"},"modified":"2025-06-04T16:09:23","kind":"lesson","parts":["<h2>If vs Whether</h2> <p><img src=\"/media/uploads/If-vs-Whether_Grammar-chart.webp\" alt=\"Grammar chart explaining the difference between 'if' and 'whether' with examples and usage rules.\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-31923\" loading=\"lazy\"></p> <h6></h6> <p>The conjunctions <strong>if</strong> and <strong>whether</strong> have similar meanings and can sometimes be used interchangeably. In this grammar lesson, you will learn when to use each one correctly.</p> <h3>Use <strong>if</strong></h3> <h4>In conditional sentences</h4> <p>We use <strong>if</strong> to express conditions in conditional sentences. It is used to introduce something that needs to happen for something else to occur. <strong>Whether</strong> is not used instead of&nbsp;<strong>if</strong> in conditional sentences.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em><span><strong>If</strong></span> you study hard, you will pass the exam.</em> <img src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"Correct\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> <li><em><span><strong>Whether</strong></span> you study hard, you will pass the exam.</em> <img src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"Wrong\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> <li><em>I would be happier <span><strong>if</strong></span> I didn’t have to work.</em> <img src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"Correct\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> <li><em>I would be happier <span><strong>whether</strong></span> I didn’t have to work.</em> <img src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"Wrong\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> </ul> <h3>Use <strong>whether</strong></h3> <p><strong>Whether</strong> is used to describe a choice between two possibilities. We use <strong>whether</strong> and not <strong>if</strong> in the following situations:</p> <h4>When there is a choice between two options or alternatives</h4> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>I couldn’t decide <span><strong>whether</strong></span> to get the red one <span><strong>or</strong></span> the green one.</em> <img src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"Correct\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> <li><em>I couldn’t decide <span><strong>if</strong></span> to get the red one <span><strong>or</strong></span> the green one.</em> <img src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"Wrong\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> </ul> <h4>Before a&nbsp;<strong>to</strong>-infinitive</h4> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>We weren’t sure <span><strong>whether to</strong></span> invite him.</em> <img src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"Correct\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> <li><em>We weren’t sure <span><strong>if</strong></span> to invite him.</em> <img src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"Wrong\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> </ul> <h4>After prepositions</h4> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>The job offer depends <span><strong>on whether</strong> </span>he passes his driving test.</em> <img src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"Correct\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> <li><em>The job offer depends <span><strong>on if</strong></span> he passes his driving test.</em> <img src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"Wrong\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> </ul> <h4>Before the words <strong>or not </strong>in sentences where only one possibility is stated</h4> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>We are still uncertain as to <span><strong>whether or not</strong></span> the request will be approved.</em> <img src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"Correct\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> <li><em>We are still uncertain as to <span><strong>if or not</strong></span> the request will be approved.</em> <img src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"Wrong\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> </ul> <h3>Use <strong>if</strong> or <strong>whether</strong></h3> <h4>To introduce clauses after stating doubt</h4> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>We aren’t sure <span><strong>if</strong></span> he’ll be able to come.</em> <img src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"Correct\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> <li><em>We aren’t sure <span><strong>whether</strong></span> he’ll be able to come.</em> <img src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"Correct\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> </ul> <h4>In indirect or reported Yes or No questions</h4> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>Do you know <span><strong>if</strong></span> John is here yet?</em> <img src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"Correct\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> <li><em>Do you know <span><strong>whether</strong></span> John is here yet?</em> <img src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"Correct\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> <li><em>I asked her <span><strong>if</strong></span> the jacket was hers.</em> <img src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"Correct\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> <li><em>I asked her <span><strong>whether</strong></span> the jacket was hers.</em> <img src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"Correct\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> </ul> <div class=\"grammar-separator-dots\"><span>Take the Quiz!</span></div> <div data-quiz=\"1239\"></div>"],"explanation":null,"quizzes":[{"id":1239,"questions":[{"id":10554,"num":"1","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>______ we don’t leave now, we’ll miss our train.</div>","choices":[{"id":19448,"letter":"A.","html":"<span> If</span>"},{"id":19449,"letter":"B.","html":"<span> Whether</span>"},{"id":19450,"letter":"C.","html":"<span> Both are correct</span>"}]},{"id":10555,"num":"2","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>We need to know ______ or not you’ll be attending the meeting.</div>","choices":[{"id":19451,"letter":"A.","html":"<span> if</span>"},{"id":19452,"letter":"B.","html":"<span> whether</span>"},{"id":19453,"letter":"C.","html":"<span> both are correct</span>"}]},{"id":10556,"num":"3","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Do you know ______ John is coming to the party?</div>","choices":[{"id":19454,"letter":"A.","html":"<span> if</span>"},{"id":19455,"letter":"B.","html":"<span> whether</span>"},{"id":19456,"letter":"C.","html":"<span> both are correct</span>"}]},{"id":10557,"num":"4","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>His final grade depends on ______ he submits the assignment on time.</div>","choices":[{"id":19457,"letter":"A.","html":"<span> if</span>"},{"id":19458,"letter":"B.","html":"<span> whether</span>"},{"id":19459,"letter":"C.","html":"<span> both are correct</span>"}]},{"id":10558,"num":"5","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I didn’t know ______ to call him.</div>","choices":[{"id":19460,"letter":"A.","html":"<span> if</span>"},{"id":19461,"letter":"B.","html":"<span> whether</span>"},{"id":19462,"letter":"C.","html":"<span> both are correct</span>"}]},{"id":10559,"num":"6","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I wasn’t sure ______ to walk or take the bus.</div>","choices":[{"id":19463,"letter":"A.","html":"<span> if</span>"},{"id":19464,"letter":"B.","html":"<span> whether</span>"},{"id":19465,"letter":"C.","html":"<span> both are correct</span>"}]},{"id":10560,"num":"7","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I’ll leave work early ______ my boss allows it.</div>","choices":[{"id":19466,"letter":"A.","html":"<span> if</span>"},{"id":19467,"letter":"B.","html":"<span> whether</span>"},{"id":19468,"letter":"C.","html":"<span> both are correct</span>"}]},{"id":10561,"num":"8","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I asked her ______ she was hungry.</div>","choices":[{"id":19469,"letter":"A.","html":"<span> if</span>"},{"id":19470,"letter":"B.","html":"<span> whether</span>"},{"id":19471,"letter":"C.","html":"<span> both are correct</span>"}]},{"id":10562,"num":"9","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>______ or not you decide to accept the offer is of little concern to me.</div>","choices":[{"id":19472,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>If</span>"},{"id":19473,"letter":"B.","html":"<span> Whether</span>"},{"id":19474,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>Both are correct</span>"}]},{"id":10563,"num":"10","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>We were arguing about ______ we should let our son attend the party.</div>","choices":[{"id":19475,"letter":"A.","html":"<span> if</span>"},{"id":19476,"letter":"B.","html":"<span> whether</span>"},{"id":19477,"letter":"C.","html":"<span> both are correct</span>"}]}]}]}